From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:19:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] main: start no helper while netifd waits for its exit

While netifd waits for its helpers on exit, netifd_start_process()
still kills the previous instance of the helper with SIGKILL before it
refuses the start. A teardown or a notify command of a protocol handler
during the wait thus kills a helper that is ending after its SIGTERM,
for example pppd before it sends its PADT. Also, uc_netifd_process()
starts new processes during the wait. These get no SIGTERM, so netifd
waits for them until procd kills it.

During the wait, refuse a helper start before any helper is killed,
and refuse process starts from ucode too.

Fixes: e4b847c71b50 ("main: wait for the helpers before exiting")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
(cherry picked from commit 2922ee823259e9b4208e0e68bfdf57a83ddb73f6)
---
 main.c   | 10 ++++++++--
 netifd.h |  1 +
 ucode.c  |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index a0479d4..49e4593 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -218,11 +218,11 @@ netifd_start_process(const char **argv, char **env, struct netifd_process *proc)
 	int pfds[2];
 	int pid;
 
-	netifd_kill_process(proc);
-
 	if (exiting)
 		return -1;
 
+	netifd_kill_process(proc);
+
 	if (pipe(pfds) < 0)
 		return -1;
 
@@ -367,6 +367,12 @@ netifd_exit_busy(void)
 	return !list_empty(&process_list) || interface_event_running();
 }
 
+bool
+netifd_exiting(void)
+{
+	return exiting;
+}
+
 void
 netifd_exit_check(void)
 {
diff --git a/netifd.h b/netifd.h
index 931b8da..a301a7f 100644
--- a/netifd.h
+++ b/netifd.h
@@ -110,6 +110,7 @@ void netifd_log_message(int priority, const char *format, ...)
 void netifd_add_process(struct netifd_process *proc, int fd, int pid);
 int netifd_start_process(const char **argv, char **env, struct netifd_process *proc);
 void netifd_kill_process(struct netifd_process *proc);
+bool netifd_exiting(void);
 void netifd_exit_check(void);
 
 struct device;
diff --git a/ucode.c b/ucode.c
index 553a72e..f5717e5 100644
--- a/ucode.c
+++ b/ucode.c
@@ -417,7 +417,7 @@ uc_netifd_process(uc_vm_t *vm, size_t nargs)
 	const char *prefix_str;
 	int pid, fd;
 
-	if (ucv_type(args) != UC_OBJECT)
+	if (ucv_type(args) != UC_OBJECT || netifd_exiting())
 		return NULL;
 
 	arg = ucv_object_get(args, "argv", NULL);
